<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar firms to 474.50/475.25/dlr.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar firms to 474.50/475.25/dlr.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar firmed for the second consecutive day to close at 474.50/475.25 per dollar as private investors continued to sell dollars for bolivars, traders said.</p>
<p>Traders attributed the dollar's fall on &quot;very attractive returns on Venezuelan assets at the moment, in fixed income instruments as well as equities,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>&quot;That's why investors are buying-up bolivars,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Traders said the Central Bank did not participate in the day's session.</p>
<p>&quot;There was no need,&quot; said another.</p>
<p>-- Silene Ramirez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
